  "intro": "Function notation $f(x)$ names a rule; $f(3)$ means substitute $3$ for $x$. Composition $f(g(x))$ applies $g$ first, then $f$. A nonlinear system pairs a line with a curve (or two curves); solve by substitution, then interpret the solutions as intersection points. A line and a parabola can meet at two points, one point (tangent), or none.",
  "items": [
